From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: msm8998: SoC provides the QUAT MI2S clocks

q6afe interprets the CPU DAI format from the DAI's own side, so CBC_CFC
(== BC_FC) configured QUAT MI2S RX with an external word select. The TAS2559
is a clock consumer as well: nothing clocked the port, the DSP accepted the
stream but never completed a buffer (hw_ptr stayed 0). Use BP_FP on the CPU
DAI and BC_FC on the codec DAI, like sdm845.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/msm8998.c	2026-10-27 01:40:34.557496404 +0800
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/msm8998.c	2026-10-27 01:40:34.586169160 +0800
@@ -360,10 +360,21 @@
 			dev_err(rtd->dev, "QUAT MI2S bclk err:%d\n", ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
+		/*
+		 * q6afe reads the format from the CPU DAI's side (as sdm845
+		 * does): BP_FP makes the port drive BCLK/WS itself. CBC_CFC
+		 * (== BC_FC) set it to wait for external clocks, which the
+		 * TAS never provides, so the DSP never consumed any data.
+		 */
 		ret = snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(cpu_dai,
-					  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC |
+					  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BP_FP |
 					  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF |
 					  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S);
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0),
+						  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BC_FC |
+						  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF |
+						  SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(rtd->dev, "QUAT MI2S fmt err:%d\n", ret);
 			snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai,
